00:00:04.070 --> 00:00:06.230 align:start position:0%
so this data was taken from the  publication modeling precision treatment  of breast cancer which was featured in  genome biology in 2013 and produced by  researchers at a company called  genentech the publication is interesting  because the authors assembled a data set  of about 50 different breast cancer cell  lines that represent the whole spectrum  of breast cancer variations the cell  lines have genomic transcriptomic and  proteomic data as well as an efficacy  measurement of commonly used and  experimental cancer drugs  if we look in the paper abstract we can  find relevant terms to this project  molecular profiles selecting features  specific to each subtype of patients and  a use case for various machine learning  methods to find answers about efficacy  of drug treatments for the right  patients  this brings me to this flow chart that  places our analysis into perspective  when we analyze data we want to answer a  question the question leads into the  data set which has to be prepared  before we even get the analysis step  or answer any of the questions we need  to know what data we are dealing with  what are its properties and how does it  describe the conditions that we are  interested in  in the next few lessons you will learn  about this type of data and the way we  can explore such data using data  visualization statistical analysis and  machine learning in python ultimately  you will see how analysis of  transcriptomic genomic or metagenomic  data can lead to important answers posed  in this publication and many other  similar projects
 

